# <type>: <subject>
# |<----  Using a Maximum Of 50 Characters  ---->|

# Explain why this change is being made
# |<----   Try To Limit Each Line to a Maximum Of 72 Characters   ---->|

# Provide links or keys to any relevant tickets, articles or other resources
# Example: Github issue #23

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be 
#    feat     (new feature)
#    fix      (bug fix)
#    refactor (refactoring code)
#    style    (formatting, missing semi colons, etc; no code change)
#    docs     (changes to documentation)
#    test     (adding or refactoring tests; no production code change)
#    chore    (updating build tasks, package manager configs, etc; no production code change)
#    perf     (performance improvement)
#    ci       (changes to CI configuration)
#    build    (changes to build system or external dependencies)
#    revert   (reverting a previous commit)
# --------------------
# Remember to:
#   - Use the imperative mood in the subject line (e.g., "Add" not "Added")
#   - Separate subject from body with a blank line
#   - Limit the subject line to 50 characters
#   - Capitalize the subject line
#   - Do not end the subject line with a period
#   - Use the body to explain what and why vs. how
#   - Wrap the body at 72 characters
#   - Reference issues and pull requests after the body
# --------------------
# Example:
#   feat: Add payment card validation
#   
#   Implement comprehensive validation for credit card inputs including
#   card number format, expiry date validation, and CVV checking.
#   
#   - Add Luhn algorithm for card number validation
#   - Implement expiry date format checking (MM/YY)
#   - Add CVV length validation (3-4 digits)
#   
#   Closes #42

